This product is a Rust port of the inference engine of Basic Pitch.

This product includes software developed at Spotify AB (http://www.spotify.com/),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
    https://github.com/spotify/basic-pitch
    Copyright 2022 Spotify AB

The model weights (ICASSP 2022) are the pretrained assets distributed with
Basic Pitch and are used unmodified. See models/basic-pitch/icassp-2022/
source_metadata.json for provenance and hashes.

This product includes software from:
  - Candle (Apache-2.0), Hugging Face: https://github.com/huggingface/candle
  - Librosa (ISC): part of the reference implementation
  - mir_eval (MIT): part of the reference implementation
  - NumPy (BSD): part of the reference implementation
  - pretty-midi (MIT): part of the reference implementation
  - resampy (ISC): part of the reference implementation
  - SciPy (BSD): part of the reference implementation
  - TensorFlow (Apache-2.0): used only to extract and validate the weights
  - Symphonia (Apache-2.0), Rust: https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia
        pure-Rust audio decoding, used by this port
  - libsoxr (LGPL-2.1-or-later): resampling, dynamically linked against the
        system library (`libsoxr.so`), resolved at build time with pkg-config

The reference implementation (Python) additionally relies on libsndfile
(LGPL-2.1-or-later) through soundfile, and on libsndfile-based decoders
for audio input. This Rust port does NOT link libsndfile: it uses
Symphonia, which is a pure-Rust decoder.

The test fixtures in basic-pitch/tests/resources include audio from the
Vocadito dataset, licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International: https://zenodo.org/record/5578807
